\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on May 30   \b0\par\par\uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2007\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, May 30 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2  GOVERNMENT MEETING   \par \par \uc2  The government will hold a regular meeting in the eastern Slovak town of Sobrance.   \par \par \uc2  TELEFONICA NEWS CONFERENCE   \par \par \uc2  Mobile phone services provider, Telefonica O2 Slovakia, to hold a news conference, 0830 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  CBANK HOLDS RATES, SIGNALS EASING PAUSE   \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) left interest rates unchanged at a policy meeting on Tuesday and signalled a pause in the current monetary policy easing as recent inflation and trade data were worse than expected.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL29581569] [RTRS-CEN-PLCY-SK]   \par \par \uc2  CBANKER: BOARD UNANIMOUS IN HOLDING RATES   \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) held interest rates at a policy meeting on Tuesday because recent economic data differed slightly from forecasts and the NBS needs more time to analyse the figures, Governor Ivan Sramko said.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nPRG000365] [RTRS-CEN-PLCY-SK]   \par \par \uc2  CBANK APRIL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  HIT 700 MLN EUROS   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday it had bought 700 million euros in one \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at curbing the crown's strength on April 4.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL29191430] [RTRS-MMT-FRX-CEN-SK]   \par \par \uc2  END-MARCH CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS SKK 0.7 BLN   \par \par \uc2  Slovakia's current account showed a preliminary surplus of 0.7 billion crowns ($27.79 million) at the end of the first quarter, compared with a gap of 23.3 billion a year ago, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nPRG000366] [RTRS-MCE-ECI-CEN-SK]   \par \par \uc2  GAS FIRM SPP 2006 PROFIT JUMPS, DIVIDENDS UP   \par \par \uc2  Slovakia's top natural gas firm  \uc2 Slovensky Plynarensky Priemysel\uc2  (SPP) reported on Tuesday a 17.6 percent jump in its net profit for 2006, and decided to pay the entire amount out in dividends.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL29658442] [RTRS-ELG-NGS-SK]   \par \par \uc2  CROWN DOWN VS EURO ON REGION, IGNORES C.BANK   \par \par \uc2  Bearish sentiment on emerging markets pushed the Slovak crown weaker against the euro on Tuesday and analysts said the unit was likely to ease further in the short-run.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL2911162] [RTRS-MMT-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2  CBANK DRAINS SKK 168 BLN IN 2-WK REPO   \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) accepted all bids in a regular two-week repo tender on Tuesday, draining 167.892 billion crowns ($6.64 billion) from the market.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL2963826] [RTRS-FRX-CEN-SK]   \par \par \uc2  END-FEB FOREIGN DEBT RISES TO $32.2 BLN   \par \par \uc2  Slovakia's gross foreign debt rose to $32.177 billion at the end of February from $31.280 billion at the end of January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL29293475] [RTRS-MMT-ECI-CEN-SK]   \par \par \uc2  PRESS DIGEST   \par \par \uc2  ------------   \par \par \uc2  CBANK DEPUTY GOVERNOR   \par \par \uc2  Viliam Ostrozlik, appointed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making board earlier this year, is the most likely candidate for the post of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor, sources who wished not to be named said.   \par \par \uc2  Pravda, page 2   \par \par \uc2  FUEL PRICES   \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Robert Fico wants to bring Slovak petrol fuel prices to the lowest level in the European Union. The government would have to cut excise taxes to achieve that goal and make fuels less expensive, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2  Sme, page 7   \par \par \uc2  SLOVAKIA, CZECH REPUBLIC, POLAND SUE EU   \par \par \uc2  Slovakia, Czech Republic and Poland will file a lawsuit against the European Commission (EC), against its fine for excess inventories of some goods.   \par \par \uc2  Sme, page 9   \par \par \uc2  AUSTRIA IMMORENT TO INVEST $238 MLN IN KOSICE   \par \par \uc2  Austria's Immorent is expected to build an industrial-logistic centre, worth 6 billion crowns ($238.2 million), in the eastern Slovak town of Kosice.   \par \par \uc2  Hospodarske Noviny, page 13   \par \par \uc2  For news on upcoming events in the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2  News editor of the day: Peter Laca, on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403   \par \par \uc2  E-mail: editorial@reuters.sk   \par \par \uc2  Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2  For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets:   \par \par \uc2  Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20>  Budapest BUX <.BUX>  Prague PX50 <.PX50>  Other related news:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\p