\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on April 25   \b0\par\par\uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2007\par 08:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, April 25 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT MEETING   \par \par \uc2 The government will hold a regular weekly meeting. Ministers are expected to debate the framework of 2008 state budget, which will set the fiscal deficit ceiling.   \par \par \uc2 PM TO ADDRESS MUNICIPALITIES   \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Robert Fico will speak at a congress of the association of Slovak municipalities.   \par \par \uc2 CROWN RISE ALLOWS SLOVAK C.BANK TO CUT RATES   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by a quarter percentage point on Tuesday, saying a firming crown and a favourable inflation outlook had made room for a second monetary policy easing in as many months.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL24666017] [RTRS-CEN-PLCY-INT-SK]   \par \par \uc2 CBANKER SAYS BOARD VOTED 7-2 TO CUT RATES   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) board voted 7-2 in favour of cutting the main two-week repo rate by 25 basis points to 4.25 percent, NBS Governor Ivan Sramko told a news conference on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nPRG000327] [RTRS-CEN-PLCY-INT-SK]   \par \par \uc2 CBANK REJECTS SOME BIDS IN 2-WK REPO TENDER   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) rejected some bids at its regular two-week repo tender on Tuesday as it continued to try and curb the strength of the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL24395770] [RTRS-CEN-FRX-INT-SK]   \par \par \uc2 GOVT SEES LOWER FISCAL GAP IN 2008   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's public finance deficit should be 2.34 percent of GDP in 2008, keeping the country on track to adopt the euro in 2009, a government outline of next year's budget showed on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL24104149] [RTRS-GVD-DBT-MCE-SK]   \par \par \uc2 KIA TO DOUBLE CAPACITY AT SLOVAK ENGINE PLANT   \par \par \uc2 Kia Motors\uc2  will invest 110 million euros to double the capacity of its engine plant in Slovakia,  \uc2 Kia Motors\uc2  Slovakia President In Kyu Bae said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL24169378] [RTRS-AUT-EUROPE-SK]   \par \par \uc2 CBANK MARCH \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  HIT 1.93BLN EUROS   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday it had bought 1.93 billion euros in two direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at curbing the crown's strength in March.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL24137251] [RTRS-CEN-MMT-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 END-FEB CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS SKK 6.9 BLN   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's current account showed a preliminary surplus of 6.9 billion crowns ($278.3 million) at the end of February, compared with a gap of 15.98 billion a year ago, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nPRG000328] [RTRS-MCE-ECI-CEN-SK]   \par \par \uc2 END-JAN FOREIGN DEBT DROPS TO $31.3 BLN   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's gross foreign debt fell to $31.280 billion at the end of January from $32.206 billion at the end of 2006, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL24336398] [RTRS-MCE-ECI-CEN-SK]   \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK TELEKOM TO PAY 2.0 BLN CROWNS IN DIVIDENDS   \par \par \uc2 The annual shareholders meeting of Slovak Telekom approved a dividend payment worth 2 billion crowns ($80.68 million), the company said in a statement on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL2450715] [RTRS-TEL-RES-SK]   \par \par \uc2 PRESS DIGEST   \par \par \uc2 ------------   \par \par \uc2 WAGE HIKE FOR DOCTORS   \par \par \uc2 The health care ministry has proposed to raise wages of doctors and nurses by 20 percent this year, but only in state-owned hospitals.   \par \par \uc2 Hospodarske Noviny, page 1   \par \par \uc2 TEACHERS' SALARIES   \par \par \uc2 Salaries of teachers will rise by several hundreds of crowns before summer break, the education ministry has ruled. The ministry expects teachers' salaries to rise further to match the average wage in Slovakia this year.   \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 1   \par \par \uc2 For news on upcoming events in the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca, on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403   \par \par \uc2 E-mail: editorial@reuters.sk   \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets:   \par \par \uc2 Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets                         [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch                        [TOP/EAST]\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on April|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|CZS|REVU|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070425e34p000j