\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on April 16   \b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2007\par 08:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, April 16 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 EU-NORM INFLATION   \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will release March EU-norm inflation data, 0700 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 FINMIN TO AUCTION 3-YR, ZERO-COUPEN STATE BOND   \par \par \uc2 The Debt and Liquidity Management Agency to auction 3-year, zero-coupon state bonds on behalf of the finance ministry.   \par \par \uc2 PSA NEWS CONFERENCE   \par \par \uc2 A Slovak unit of the French car maker  \uc2 PSA Peugeot\uc2 Peugeot Citroen\uc2  will hold a news conference on the plant's 2006 results and 2007 perspectives, 0800 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 INTERVIEW-SLOVAK DEFICIT WON'T BUST TARGET-FINANCE MINISTER   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's government will do all it can to ensure the country adopts the euro in 2009 as planned, and fears the fiscal deficit target may be busted are unfounded, Finance Minister Jan Pociatek said on Saturday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nWBT006812] [RTRS-EEU-GVD-DBT-SK]   \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY MINISTER WINS NO-CONFIDENCE VOTE   \par \par \uc2 Slovak Economy Minister Lubomir Jahnatek survived a no-confidence vote on Friday as the three-party ruling coalition united to win its first major challenge in parliament despite several internal quarrels.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL13242059] [RTRS-EUROPE-POL-SK]   \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES JUMP AFTER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBS) foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped to $17.578 billion as of April 11 from $16.564 billion a week ago, the bank said on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nPRG000308] [RTRS-CEN-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 CROWN REBOUNDS FROM 1-WK LOWS VS EURO   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown erased early losses against the euro on Friday, rebounding from one-week lows, but dealers said its short-term direction was unclear due to a lack of impetus.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL132082] [RTRS-MMT-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 PRESS DIGEST   \par \par \uc2 ------------   \par \par \uc2 FINMIN SEES NO CHANGES TO TAX-SYSTEM IN 2008   \par \par \uc2 The government will not alter the tax system in 2008, daily Pravda cited the Finance Ministry's Deputy Minister Vladimir Palko as saying. Palko said he saw no risk on the side of revenues threatening Slovakia's goal to adopt the euro in 2009.   \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 1   \par \par \uc2 For news on upcoming events in the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca, on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403   \par \par \uc2 E-mail: editorial@reuters.sk   \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets:   \par \par \uc2 Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets 