\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on April 10   \b0\par\par\uc2 761 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2007\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, April 105 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT   \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will publish February industrial output data (0700 GMT). Analysts forecast industrial output growth of 18.0 percent, year-on-year.   \par \par \uc2 RETAIL SALES   \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will publish February retail sales data (0700 GMT). Analysts forecast retail sales to have risen by 5.0 percent, year-on-year.   \par \par \uc2 CONSTRUCTION OUTPUT   \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will publish February construction output data (0700 GMT).   \par \par \uc2 INDUSTRIAL WAGES   \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will publish February average industrial wage data (0700 GMT).   \par \par \uc2 REPO TENDER   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its regular liquidity draining two-week repo tender.   \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA WELL PLACED TO ADOPT EURO IN 2009-OECD   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia is well placed to adopt the euro in 2009 as planned, the OECD said on Thursday, though it urged the authorities to remain on guard against inflation risks.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL0528230] [RTRS-FRX-POL-CEN-SK]   \par \par \uc2 CBANKER SAYS SKK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  EFFECTIVE   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rise of the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday morning was effective, board member Peter Sevcovic told Reuters on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL05104387] [RTRS-CEN-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 OECD CHIEF SEES U.S. SLOWING, RATE CUT POSSIBLE   \par \par \uc2 U.S. economic growth will slow by about one percentage point to about 2.2-2.3 percent this year and the Federal Reserve may ease interest rates in the Autumn, OECD Secretary General Angel Gurria said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nPRA001234] [RTRS-FED-CEN-INT-SK]   \par \par \uc2 OECD CHIEF:NO ROOM FOR EURO ZONE RATES AT 4.25 PCT   \par \par \uc2 Underlying inflation in the euro zone does not signal a great danger at this stage and interest rates are not likely to rise to 4.25 percent, OECD Secretary General Angel Gurria said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL05249848] [RTRS-EMRG-WEU-EEU-SK]   \par \par \uc2 CROWN QUIET BEFORE HOLIDAY, SEEN STRONGER   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown hugged a tight range around the 33.400 level to the euro Thursday, as investors squared positions ahead of Easter holiday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL05252220] [RTRS-MMR-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES DROP TO $16.564 BLN   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBS) foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves edged down to $16.564 billion as of April 3 from $16.587 billion the previous week, the bank said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL05213410] [RTRS-CEN-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 PRESS DIGEST   \par \par \uc2 ------------   \par \par \uc2 TRANSPETROL CASE   \par \par \uc2 Foreign assets of the stricken Russian oil firm YUKOS, including the 49 percent stake in the Slovak oil pipeline operator Transpetrol, are set for an auction starting on May 10. The Slovak government has been trying to buy back the Transpetrol stake.   \par \par \uc2 Hospodarske Noviny, page 1   \par \par \uc2 CHEAPER GAS UNLIKELY   \par \par \uc2 Prices of natural gas for households are unlikely to decline due to high cost of oil on world markets. The state regulator said earlier this year it expected cheaper gas in the second half of the year.   \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 1   \par \par \uc2 LABOUR CODE DRAFT   \par \par \uc2 The government will delay its debate on labour code amendments until April 18, due to longer-than-expected negotiations on the final version of the draft.   \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 1   \par \par \uc2 MOTION TO DISMISS ECONOMY MINISTER   \par \par \uc2 Opposition deputies will submit on Tuesday a proposal to dismiss Economy Minister Lubomir Jahnatek. The opposition has accused Jahnatek of promoting corruption in state arms makers. Jahnatek has rejected the accusations.   \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 2   \par \par \uc2 FICO POSTPONES LATAM VISIT   \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Robert Fico has delayed his visit to Latin America, which he was expected to begin on Tuesday, due to flu.   \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 1   \par \par \uc2 For news on upcoming events in the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca, on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403   \par \par \uc2 E-mail: editorial@reuters.sk   \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: pater.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets:   \par \par \uc2 Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\par  TO