\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Cautious pre-US data; risk appetite on the up   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Agnieszka Flak   \par \uc2 954 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2007\par 13:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Please note that there will not be an emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  report from London on Friday April 6 and Monday April 9 due to the Good Friday and Easter holidays.)   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, April 5 (Reuters) - Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shuffled in tight ranges on Thursday despite a rebound in risk appetite, with many investors cautious ahead of U.S. jobs data that could shed light on the health of the world's biggest economy.   \par \par \uc2 Markets have calmed down as the release of 15 captive British sailors by Iran soothed fears of a standoff between Tehran and the West. Emerging equities <.MSCIEF> jumped 0.2 percent to a new record high, beating levels hit before a Feb 27 fall in China helped trigger a two-week global selloff.   \par \par \uc2 Now, the focus has shifted back to the U.S. economy, after recent data did little to sway expectations the Federal Reserve will cut interest rates later in the year but left the potential timing of such a move uncertain.   \par \par \uc2 "The theme today is that high-yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are stronger...the carry theme is alive and kicking," said Olivier Desbarres, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse in London.   \par \par \uc2 "Risk appetite is back -- all the indicators confirm that."   \par \par \uc2 But Desbarres said strong growth in the euro area and the rest of the world posed the risk that the market was overpricing the possibility of a rate cut by the Federal Reserve and underpricing posible monetary tightening elsewhere.   \par \par \uc2 "For now equities and high yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are benefiting, but there is a risk the market is being too complacent about Fed rate cuts and the possibility of monetary tightening globally," he added.   \par \par \uc2 But for now high yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were faring well.   \par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira <TRY=> was up nearly 0.4 percent at 1.37 per dollar, matching an 11-month high hit in the previous session. Traders said however there is potential for volatility in the run-up to elections this summer.   \par \par \uc2 South Africa's <ZAR=> rand eased 0.3 percent versus the dollar as traders took profits off a run to five-week highs. The rand will likely be rangebound ahead of an April 12 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting which may deliver a 50 basis point interest rate rise.   \par \par \uc2 THIN VOLUMES   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said volumes were thinner than usual, with the risk some investors might take profits on emerging market trades before the long weekend. Many central European markets are closed on Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown stayed weak after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down one percent. By 1045 GMT it had eased 0.2 percent to 33.42 per euro <EURSKK=>, off the two-week high around 33.100 per euro hit just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in.   \par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty firmed 0.10 percent to 3.84 per euro and dealers said a close below that level would open the door for a strong zloty next week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a three-month high on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Investors will be watching closely the U.S. non-farm payrolls data due on Friday. The U.S. economy is expected to have added 120,000 jobs in March, up from 97,000 in February, according to a Reuters poll of analysts.   \par \par \uc2 Carsten Fritsch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in Frankfurt, said a very soft number would hit recovering risk appetite.   \par \par \uc2 "If we get some very soft U.S. data causing fears of    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recession...or some geopolitical stuff from Iran or other areas\par which could cause high risk aversion...then the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par move and we might see a correction," he said.\par   Additional reporting by Sujata Rao and Jamie McGeever\par \par \par  [20070405 110808 GMT] \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 LATEST    PREV   LOCAL    LOCAL  \par                                 CLOSE  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                        PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par                                                 IN 2007\par  EUROPE/MIDDLE EAST/AFRICA\par  Czech Rep.   <EURCZK=>   27.92     27.92   -0.03    -1.59\par  Poland       <EURPLN=>    3.84      3.84   +0.10    -0.26\par  Hungary      <EURHUF=>  245.66    245.51   -0.06    +2.23\par  Slovakia     <EURSKK=>   33.46     33.37   -0.28    +2.87\par  Romania      <EURRON=>    3.33      3.33   -0.02    +1.40\par  Ukraine      <UAH=>       5.04      5.06   +0.34    +0.14\par  South Africa <ZAR=>       7.13      7.13   -0.06    -2.01\par  Kenya        <KES=>      68.95     69.25   +0.44    +0.87\par  Israel       <ILS=>       4.14      4.13   -0.18    +1.85\par  Turkey       <TRY=>       1.37      1.37   +0.14    +3.35\par  \par  LATAM\par  Mexico       <MXN=>      11.01     11.01   +0.03    -1.91\par  Brazil       <BRL=>       2.03      2.03   +0.00    +4.94\par  Venezuela    <VEB=>    2144.60   2144.60   +0.00    +0.00\par  Chile        <CLP=>     537.70    537.70   +0.00    -1.04\par  \par  ASIA\par  Singapore    <SGD=