\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbanker says SKK  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  effective   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Dokoupil   \par \uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2007\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotes, analyst comment, background)   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, April 5 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rise of the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday morning was effective, board member Peter Sevcovic told Reuters on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Sevcovic also said the NBS agreed with the OECD that energy prices are among key risks to Slovakia meeting the EU's inflation criterion to adopt the euro as planned in 2009, though the bank was not worried by a recent spike in oil prices.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was certainly effective because the exchange rate depreciated slightly," he said on the sidelines of a presentation of the OECD's report on Slovakia, adding the bank was prepared to act further if needed.   \par \par \uc2 "Every \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is effective, because you never know whether the exchange rate would have fallen to 32.0 (per euro) if we had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the NBS started selling crowns on the market early on Wednesday when it traded at around 33.100 per euro, its strongest level since March 20 when the NBS last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The bank said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the crown's increased volatility and "unjustified" moves in recent days.   \par \par \uc2 But it did not comment on the details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which weakened the crown as far as 33.700 per euro. The unit traded at 33.465 as of 1040 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was correct because the firming of the crown over the past weeks, and past few days was too fast when compared to economic developments," Sevcovic said.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep monitoring, assessing and reacting (to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market developments)," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS has repeatedly said the crown should move around the ERM-2 central rate of 35.4424 per euro, which it regards as near the equilibrium level justified by economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 "The fact that market players seem to be reluctant to push EUR/SKK lower prevents the pair from moving further south today," said 4Cast analyst Piotr Matys.   \par \par \uc2 "But next week we expect the crown to recover further on the back of domestic data and positive sentiment in the region which means the NBS will be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again when the pair falls to around 33.10," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The strong crown has helped the NBS to curb inflation. It cut the main two-week repo rate by 25 basis points to 4.50 percent at the end of March after the rising crown tightened monetary conditions.   \par \par \uc2 Sevcovic also said inflation risks stemming from high oil prices have decreased with changes in consumption.   \par \par \uc2 "It is still one of the most serious risks. But if you look one or two years back, energy had a weighting of 22-25 percent in the consumer basket, but ... it's only 17 percent now," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "If the average oil price is around $75 a barrel ... we are still meeting everything without problems with inflation at 1.8 percent and this does not worry us," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS predicts end-year inflation using the EU measure at 1.5 percent, below February's record low of 2.0 percent, assuming an average oil price of $65 a barrel, Sevcovic said. The bank will present new forecasts on April 27.   \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA-CROWN/CBANKER (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|CZS|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070408e3450006c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
