\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak cbank says to keep curbing crown crown   \b0\par\par\uc2 107 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2007\par 09:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, April 4 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday due to increased crown volatility and its unjustified firming in recent days.   \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member, Karol Mrva, told Reuters the bank remained prepared to correct unwanted crown moves in the future.   \par \par \uc2 Mrva also reiterated a warning to investors that the crown's conversion rate to the euro, which is expected to be set at around mid-2008, may differ from market levels at that time.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA/CBANK (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|CZS|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070404e344000ih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
