\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to curb crown   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Laca   \par \uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2007\par 08:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds NBS Governor, analyst comments)   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, April 4 (Reuters) - The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) fought again to curb the crown's strength with a second market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in as many weeks on Wednesday, and warned it would continue to correct unwanted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers in Bratislava said the NBS started selling crowns on the market early on Wednesday when it traded at around 33.100 per euro, its strongest level since March 20 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The bank confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it was because of the crown's increased volatility and "unjustified" moves in recent days.   \par \par \uc2 "We are prepared to act in the same way in the future," NBS board member Karol Mrva told Reuters. "If we see too sharp volatility and unjustified moves we are willing and prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 The NBS would not comment on the details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which weakened the crown as far as 33.700 per euro <EURSKK=>. The unit traded at 33.440 as of 1450 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 NBS Governor Ivan Sramko told reporters that the crown's strength remained excessive: "We are consistently stating that we will use all tools because we think that the crown's exchange rate is overvalued."   \par \par \uc2 The crown reached a record high of 32.710 after its peg in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism, the precursor to euro adoption, was revalued by 8.5 percent on March 16.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS has repeatedly said the crown should move around the new ERM-2 central rate of 35.4424 per euro, which it sees to be near the equilibrium level justified by economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 The strong crown has helped the NBS to curb inflation, aiding Slovakia's aim of entering the euro zone in 2009.   \par \par \uc2 The NBS cut its main two-week repo rate by 25 basis points to 4.50 percent at the end of March after the rising crown effectively tightened monetary conditions.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased prospects of a further interest rate cut by 25 basis points this month," said Lucia Steklacova, a senior analyst at ING Bank.   \par \par \uc2 The crown has been rising on the back of accelerating economic growth, which is expected to surpass last year's 8.3 percent in 2007, and because investors expect to profit from further appreciation before euro adoption.   \par \par \uc2 Mrva reiterated a warning that the crown's conversion rate to the euro, which is expected to be set at around mid-2008, may differ from market levels at that time.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared determined not to let the crown rise too far but analysts said it would probably manage only to slow its climb.   \par \par \uc2 "The crown has potential to firm further due to fundamentals in a longer term ... benefiting from higher economic growth and productivity gains," said Maria Valachyova, senior analyst at Slovenska Sporitelna.   \par \par \uc2 "We see the final conversion rate at 32.50, which could be an equilibrium level when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be fixed (to the euro) roughly in the mid-2008," she said.   \par \par \uc2 Some market watchers said NBS \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated to be worth between 2-3 billion euros in total so far this year, were increasing investors' exposure to the crown, which could make the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more vulnerable to global capital flows.   \par \par \uc2 "The crown might become more sensitive to shake-ups on emerging markets, although Slovak fundamentals are good," said Miroslav Plojhar, chief economist at Citibank Czech Republic. (Additional reporting by Martin Santa)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|CZS|BNX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070404e344000ef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
