\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on April 2   \b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2007\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, April 2 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 STATE BUDGET DATA   \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry will publish central state budget data for January-March.   \par \par \uc2 STATE BOND AUCTION   \par \par \uc2 The Debt and Liquidity Management Agency will auction 10-year, 4.2 percent state bond, by 1000 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA QUESTIONS EU UNITY ON KOSOVO   \par \par \uc2 Slovakia on Saturday challenged the idea that the European Union was united behind a plan for Kosovo's independence and said it would work to ensure Serbia's concerns were taken into account at the United Nations.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL31712781] [RTRS-EU-DIP-POL-BAK]   \par \par \uc2 CAR MAKERS SLAM GOVT LABOUR CODE PLANS   \par \par \uc2 Slovak car makers on Friday attacked government plans for more job protection as a threat to competitiveness and growth.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL30428918] [RTRS-AUT-JOB-POL-SK]   \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES JUMP AFTER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBS) foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped to $16.587 billion as of March 28 from $14.771 billion the previous week, the bank said on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nPRG000289] [RTRS-CEN-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 CROWN STRONGER, EYES CBANK REPO FOR TREND   \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown was stronger against the euro on Friday thanks to a positive mood on central European markets, and investors waited for a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signal about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL30382237] [RTRS-MMT-FRX-SK]   \par \par \uc2 PRESS DIGEST   \par \par \uc2 ------------   \par \par \uc2 ETHNIC HUNGARIANS CHANGE LEADER   \par \par \uc2 Pal Csaky surprisingly beat Bela Bugar to become the leader of the ethnic Hungarian party SMK. Some ruling coalition politicians said they feared more radical views from the opposition SMK, but analysts said that was unlikely to occur.   \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 1   \par \par \uc2 SLOTA SLAMS U.S. FOREIGN POLICY   \par \par \uc2 Jan Slota, the leader of the right-wing Slovak National Party, a junior coalition member, has slammed foreign policy of the United States, saying Washington was destroying entire nations.   \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 2   \par \par \uc2 NO TRUST IN UNIONS   \par \par \uc2 Majority of employees in Slovakia do not trust trade unions, a poll conducted by a private agency FOCUS showed. The workers polled by Focus said unions cannot not protect the employees' rights.   \par \par \uc2 Hospodarske Noviny, page 1   \par \par \uc2 For news on upcoming events in the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca, on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403   \par \par \uc2 E-mail: editorial@reuters.sk   \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: pater.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]