\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown weakens, mkt prepares for rate cut  \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 16:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, March 23 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown weakened by 0.6 percent versus the euro on Friday as investors cut local exposure to take profits and prepared positions for an expected interest rate cut, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The crown <EURSKK=> was at 33.575 to the euro as of 1525 GMT, compared with 33.375 seen late on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The crown had a volatile week, first jumping on revaluation of its parity rate in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism, then erasing part of the gains due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the rally.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit rose by over 3 percent after the ERM-2 parity shift, hitting a record high of 32.710 per euro on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying the new parity rate of 35.4424 per euro was near the equilibrium level justified by economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 The market now expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) to cut interest rates at the monthly monetary policy meeting on March 27, according to a Reuters poll of analysts.  \par \par \uc2 "The Slovak crown could come under pressure next week, because of the NBS's meeting and possible rate reduction by as much as 50 basis points," said Komercni Banka analysts.  \par \par \uc2 Some market watchers, however, said the rate decision would be a close call and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might keep the main two-week repo rate unchanged at 4.75 percent because of persisting inflation risks from energy prices. ------------------ MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1525 GMT ----------------- Crown/euro <EURSKK=> at 33.575 vs 33.370 on Thursday Crown/dollar <SKK=> at 25.242 vs 24.955 5-yr govt bond <SK5YT=RR> yield 4.242/4.002 pct vs 4.227/4.007 7-yr govt bond <SK7YT=RR> yield 4.394/4.194 pct vs 4.209/3.988 ---------------------------------------------------------------  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA-CROWN/AFTERNOON|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|CZS|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070323e33n001hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
