\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown flat, seen stabilising after jumps  \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 10:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, March 22 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown was little changed on Thursday morning after a roller coaster ride earlier this week caused by a shift of its peg to the euro within the ERM-2 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers saw the crown stabilising at around current levels in the near future as the market waited for fresh impetus from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy meeting on March 27.  \par \par \uc2 The crown traded at 33.370 to the euro as of 0845 GMT, flat from late on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "For the next few days, at least until the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's meeting next Tuesday, we do not expect attempts to move the crown to the stronger side, but rather calmer wait-and-see trading," Slovenska Sporitelna analysts said in a market note.  \par \par \uc2 The crown jumped by over 3 percent on Monday, reaching an all-time high of 32.710 per euro, after its parity rate in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism was revalued by 8.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and flooded the money market with crown liquidity on Tuesday to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 NBS's action has weakened the local unit, but Governor Ivan Sramko repeated on Wednesday the crown remained overvalued and that the bank would use its tools to move it to levels justified by economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA-CROWN/MORNING|LANGEN|CZS|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument L