\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia Revalues Its ERM II Euro Peg To 35.4424  \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 08:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Corrected March 19, 2007 04:15 ET (08:15 GMT) [ 19-03-07 0801GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia has revalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 8.5% against the euro as the country heads for the euro-zone accession.  \par \par \uc2 The new parity rate - the level at which the koruna is pegged against the euro in the European Exchange Rate Mechanism, or ERM II - is set at SKK35.4424, with fluctuations in the koruna restricted to no more than 15% above or below this rate.  \par \par \uc2 The previous parity rate, set in late 2005, was SKK38.4550 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 As reported late last week, when the parity change was first unveiled by the European Commission, the koruna's new peg against the euro will help the Slovak government to keep its economy stable as it aims to adopt the euro in 2009. [ 19-03-07 0819GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 At 0830 GMT, the koruna was trading at SKK32.02 against the euro, from SKK32.99 earlier Monday and SKK33.8 late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also set the new minimum and maximum levels at which it is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the koruna from further firming or weakening at SKK30.1260 and SKK40.7588 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak koruna has appreciated significantly, fueled by solid foreign direct investment inflows.  \par \par \uc2 The country's stellar economic growth of 8.3% on the year in 2006 and 6% a year earlier has also bolstered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times since mid-2006 to slow the strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Some markets participants expected the bank to consider revaluing the koruna-euro parity peg to create more breathing room for itself.  \par \par \uc2 Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 :  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.nbs.sk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.nbs.sk }}}\par \par \uc2 -By Leos Rousek, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 221 085 273; leos.rousek@dowjones.com [ 19-03-07 0838GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070319e33j0008n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
