\par\par \b \uc2 FOCUS: Slovak Koruna Revalution Lifts Other CEE Units  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leos Rousek and Joel Sherwood  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 16:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   PRAGUE (Dow Jones)-Eastern European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bounced higher Monday after Slovakia revalued the koruna by 8.5%, sparking speculation that similar moves in the region could follow.  The Czech koruna, Polish zloty and Hungarian forint led gains elsewhere. The forint rose nearly 2% against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as markets speculated that the Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would adjust its own, self-devised trading bands.   The standout exception was Latvia, where the Lat continued to come under pressure amid concerns the economy was overheating. The Baltic country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was forced to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday morning with Lat purchases in the open market to strut the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   Slovak authorities, the European Commission and the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late Friday agreed that the Slovak koruna should trade in a new band with the E.U.'s Exchange Rate Mechanism II.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the koruna from firming above SKK30.1260 against the euro, or weakening below SKK40.7588 to the euro. In the region, Slovakia, Latvia, Estonia are considered to be within three years of joining the euro zone. As an interim step, they belong to the ERM II system of fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading ranges versus the euro. Hungary has a reference trading of its own devising. Appreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are all good news for the region hoping to keep exports competitive, say economists. The Slovak revaluation was "good news for Slovakia: the economy is growing at near-Chinese rates, and a revaluation, two years ahead of euro entry, is better now than later," said Maya Bhandari at Lombard Street Research. "It isn't such good news for some of other CEE \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted by the stronger koruna - the HUF now looks seriously dear." Countries that wish to join the euro zone must spend at least two years in the ERM, keeping their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a 15% range above or below a central exchange rate against the euro. The koruna has appreciated more rapidly than the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other countries that joined the European Union in 2004. While the Slovak koruna has appreciated by 10% since late 2005, the Czech koruna has strengthened by 3.8%, and the Polish zloty and Hungarian forint have each appreciated by 2.4%. The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength has come on continued foreign investment, in particular large car manufacturers accessing a qualified and cheap pool of labor, said Beat Siegenthaler, an economist at TD Securities in London. The Latvian Lat, by contrast, has come under unremitting pressure. Lars Christensen, senior analyst at Danske Bank, says the Latvian government needs to do more to control mounting economic imbalances fueled by rampant domestic credit growth of 56% in 2006. "It's worrisome in the sense that it's an indication of the erosion of the credibility of the peg," says Christensen, but added, "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only do so much."  \par \par \uc2 By Leos Rousek, of Dow Jones Newswires; leos.rousek@dowjones.com, +420-221-085-272 [ 03-19-07 1152ET ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070319e33j0003x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
