\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown holds near highs, eyes region, cbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, March 16 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown held flat near record highs on Friday as investors waited for an impetus from bigger markets amid a lack of domestic factors, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The crown traded at 33.970 per euro <EURSKK=> as of 0845 GMT, little changed from 33.945 late on Thursday and just 0.5 percent off its all-time high of 33.8 per euro from March 8.  \par \par \uc2 "With no local data today, we look towards global market sentiment to drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so the U.S. inflation data will be of utmost importance in this respect," KBC Bank wrote in a market note.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. inflation data are due at 1230 GMT. The most closely watched figure will likely be core consumer price inflation for February which is expected to rise 0.2 percent on the month.  \par \par \uc2 Traders saw the crown drifting near 34.0 per euro level in the near term, expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent sharp firming.  \par \par \uc2 "One thing is clear -- the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen below EUR/SKK 33.80 at the moment," KBC said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to halt the crown rise when the unit hit its record highs one week ago. ------------------ MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0845 GMT ----------------- Crown/euro <EURSKK=> 33.970 vs 33.945 on Thursday (-0.07 pct) Crown/dollar <SKK=> at 25.510 vs 25.629 (+0.47 pct) 5-yr govt bond <SK5YT=RR> yield 4.237/4.071 vs 4.413/4.013 pct 7-yr govt bond <SK7YT=RR> yield 4.289/4.156 vs 4.242/4.159 pct ------------------------