\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on March 9  \b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, March 9 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 SDKU ON LABOUR CODE  \par \par \uc2 The largest opposition party SDKU will hold a news conference on prepared changes to Slovakia's labour code, 10.30 a.m. (0930 GMT).  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES DATA  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will publish weekly foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data, 2 p.m. (1300 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 CROWN HITS NEW RECORD, C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market on Thursday to halt firming of the crown after news of foreign direct investment inflows and accelerating economic growth drove the unit to new record highs.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL08455761] [RTRS-MMT-FRX-EUR-SK]  \par \par \uc2 SAMSUNG CONFIRMS SLOVAKIA SITE FOR NEW LCD PLANT  \par \par \uc2 Samsung Electronics Co. Ltd. , the world's biggest maker of large liquid crystal displays, said on Thursday it picked Slovakia as the site for a new LCD panel assembly plant.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nSEO348231] [RTRS-ELC-ELI-ENT-SK]  \par \par \uc2 BISHOPS DEFEND ARCHBISHOP ON SPY REPORTS  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's Catholic bishops on Thursday rejected allegations in a newspaper that Archbishop Jan Sokol had collaborated with the country's communist-era secret police force.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL08569606] [RTRS-REL-EUROPE-SK]  \par \par \uc2 PRESS DIGEST  \par \par \uc2 -------------  \par \par \uc2 GABCIKOVO DEAL  \par \par \uc2 Sklovakia's Attorney General said the contract under which Slovenske Elektrarne, owned by Italy's Enel , rents the country's largest hydro power plant Gabcikovo is invalid.  \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 1  \par \par \uc2 COALITION QUARRELS  \par \par \uc2 Problems have piled up inside the ruling coalition as its three leaders have not held a formal meeting for two months. The three ruling coalition parties have clashed over several issues in recent weeks, including \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of their ministries, changes to labour code or foreign policy.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 1  \par \par \uc2 LABOUR SHORTAGE  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's Samsung Electronics , which has just announced a plan to build its new LCD panel plant near the western Slovak town of Trnava, may face labour shortage problems as it will operate in a region with low unemployment rate. Analysts also expected upward pressures on wages in the region.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 3  \par \par \uc2 UNION PROTESTS  \par \par \uc2 Steel industry trade unions plan to organise protest rallies against employers' opposition to the prepared labour code changes.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 7  \par \par \uc2 For news on upcoming events in the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca, on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: editorial@reuters.sk  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       