\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown stronger, seen testing firmer levels   \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2007\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown hovered in sight of seven-week highs against the euro in early trade on Wednesday with dealers expecting it to test even stronger levels in the coming days amid positive regional sentiment.   \par \par \uc2 The crown traded at 34.285 to the euro <EURSKK=> as of 0840 GMT, from 34.330 late on Tuesday and 0.2 percent down from a seven-week high of 34.210 per euro hit in the previous session.   \par \par \uc2 The crown rose to hit its strongest levels since December 28 on Tuesday, driven by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to accept all bids in its liquidity draining repo tender, but failed to build on gains as investors took quick profits.   \par \par \uc2 "The crown is stable," one Bratislava-based dealer said. "The crown might test lower (firmer) levels, as yesterday's repo tender might be seen as a signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will let the unit move to 34.0 per euro."   \par \par \uc2 The NBS rejected bids in the repo tender to leave the market flooded with excess funds at the beginning of the year to stem the crown, which hit a record of 34.05 per euro in December, a level where directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading 10.9 percent above its parity rate in the exchange rate mechanism ERM-2, which Slovaks entered in November 2005 as part of its strategy to adopt the euro in 2009. ------------------ MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0840 GMT ----------------- Crown/euro <EURSKK=> 34.285 vs 34.330 on Tuesday (+0.15) Crown/dollar <SKK=> 26.065 vs 26.125 (+0.33) 5-yr govt bond <SK5YT=RR> yield 4.300/4.150