\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Jan 31  \b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2007\par 08:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Jan 31 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press repors and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT MEETING  \par \par \uc2 The government will hold a regular weekly meeting. The cabinet is expected to vote on a nominee for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice-governor.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK HOLDS RATES, IN NO RUSH TO CUT  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) left interest rates unchanged for the fourth consecutive month on Tuesday and signalled it would not rush to ease policy despite an improved inflation outlook.  \par \par \uc2 [nL30425463] [RTRS-CEN-INT-PLCY-SK]  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK VOTED ON RATE CUT, MAJORITY AGAINST  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board voted on a proposal to cut interest rates by 25 basis points on Tuesday but a majority was in favour of no change, Governor Ivan Sramko said.  \par \par \uc2 [nPRG000214] [RTRS-CEN-PLCY-INT-SK]  \par \par \uc2 CBANK BOUGHT EUR 495 MLN IN DEC \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday it bought 495 million euros in December direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at curbing the crown's strength.  \par \par \uc2 [nPRG000217] [RTRS-CEN-MMT-FRX-SK]  \par \par \uc2 CROWN STEADY VS EURO AFTER C.BANK STAYS PUT  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown was little changed against the euro on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) left interest rates on hold for the fourth month in a row, and dealers saw it moving without a clear trend in the short term.  \par \par \uc2 [nL30220462] [RTRS-MMT-FRX-SK]  \par \par \uc2 CBANK ACCEPTS ALL BIDS IN REPO TENDER  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) accepted all bids made in a regular two-week repo tender on Tuesday, after leaving banks with excess liquidity for the previous four weeks to cap the crown's rise.  \par \par \uc2 [nL30402890] [RTRS-CEN-INT-MMT-SK]  \par \par \uc2 JAN-NOV C/A GAP WIDENS Y/Y TO SKK 121 BLN  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's current account showed a preliminary deficit of 121.3 billion crowns ($4.45 billion) for the first 11 months of 2006, up from an 82.96 billion gap the previous year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 [nPRG000216] [RTRS-TRD-ECI-MCE-SK]  \par \par \uc2 END-OCT FOREIGN DEBT WIDENS TO $30.46 BLN  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's gross foreign debt edged up to $30.459 billion at the end of October from $29.336 billion at the end of September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 [nL30621601] [RTRS-GVD-DBT-SK]  \par \par \uc2 PRESS DIGEST  \par \par \uc2 ------------  \par \par \uc2 AUSTRIAN AIRLINES PULLS OUT FROM SLOVAK AIRLINES  \par \par \uc2 Austrian Airlines said it had pulled out from the Slovak Airlines, which subsequently halted all regular flights. Austrian Airlines' move came after the Slovak government failed to assume debts of the Slovak airliner.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 7  \par \par \uc2 ORCO TO INVEST 100 MLN EURO IN SLOVAKIA  \par \par \uc2 Real estate developer Orco Property Group said it would invest 100 million euro ($129.6 million) in Slovakia's capital Bratislava to build offices and apartments.  \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 1  \par \par \uc2 DOCTORS' WAGES SEEN UP FROM JULY  \par \par \uc2 Healthcare Minister Ivan Valentovic said the ministry had proposed to raise wages of doctors and nurses by 9 percent from July. Doctors' Union has recently criticised the government for not meeting a promise of a 30 percent wage increase.  \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 3  \par \par \uc2 EURO PLENIPOTENTIARY  \par \par \uc2 The cabinet of Prime Minister Robert Fico is expected to name \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat as its plenipotentiary for euro adoption.  \par \par \uc2 Hospodarske Noviny, page 5  \par \par \uc2 United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: editorial@reuters.sk  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: martin.dokoupil.reuters.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets                         [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch                        [TOP/EAST]\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Jan 31|LANGEN|Table|CZS|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|REVU|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070131e31v000tb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
