\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank bought EUR 495 mln in Dec  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 132 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2007\par 14:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Jan 30 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Tuesday it bought 495 million euros in December direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at curbing the crown's strength.  \par \par \uc2 The crown, the fastest rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in central Europe last year, firmed to an all-time high of 34.050 per euro on Dec. 28, prompting the NBS to step in the market. Traders have estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume at around 500 million euros.  \par \par \uc2 The crown has lost 3.5 percent against the euro since then, hit by weak regional sentiment and NBS efforts to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. It was quoted at 35.250 per euro <EURSKK=> as of 1332 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA-CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|D|M|CZS|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070130e31u001kn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
