\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Slovak cbank sold 1.75 bln euros on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mkt in July  \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2006\par 14:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds background on curency, current crown level)  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) sold 1.750 billion euros in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in July aimed at defending the crown against weakening pressures, the NBS said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The crown fell after a June 17 election as negative sentiment on emerging markets combined with investors worries the new leftist Slovak government will loosen fiscal policy and cause a delay in euro adoption from the target year of 2009.  \par \par \uc2 The bank also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the market in June to the tune of 1.335 billion euros. The total amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and July was in line with analysts estimates of around 3 billion euros.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown has since stabilised and pared most of the losses from the post-election turbulence, helped by government assurances that adopting the euro in 2009 will be a top priority.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by 50 basis points in July to fight off inflation risks, which also made investment into crown more attractive.  \par \par \uc2 The crown currently trades at 37.730 to the euro, around 2.5 percent stronger from levels of around 38.700 where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July.  \par \par \uc2 The crown has been locked in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism, a waiting room for euro adoption, since November 2005 and the country must fulfil a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability criterion to be allowed to enter the euro zone.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also needs a firming \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help it slash inflation by early 2008 as Slovakia sticks to its euro adoption timetable.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|CZS|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060825e28p000yv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
