\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on July 24  \b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2006\par 09:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 24 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK SEEN LIFTING RATES BY 50 BPS IN JULY  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to raise interest rates by 50 basis points next week, its third increase this year to head off rising inflation risks, a Reuters poll showed on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL21484057]  \par \par \uc2 CBANK RESERVES DROP ON CROWN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped sharply in the week to July 19, data released on Friday showed, raising questions over the bank's ability to ward off a speculative attack on the crown.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL21532193]  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES DROP TO $13.06 BLN  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $13.060 billion in the week to July 19, from $15.466 billion one week earlier, the bank said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nPRA000026]  \par \par \uc2 CROWN EASES ON \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES FALL  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown lost ground versus the euro on Friday after a drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves raised questions about its ability to fend off a speculative attack.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL21794427]  \par \par \uc2 HUNGARIANS OPPRESS SLOVAKS, NATIONALISTS SAY  \par \par \uc2 Jan Slota, the leader of the far-right Slovak National Party (SNS) said the ethnic Hungarians were oppressing the Slovak majority, the daily Pravda reports. SNS is a junior member of Prime Minister Robert Fico's ruling coalition.  \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 2  \par \par \uc2 ECONMIN DISCUSSES TRANSPETROL SALE  \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Lubomir Jahnatek will travel to Russian to meet YUKOS and Russneft officials and discuss the sale of the 49 percent stake in Slovakia's oil pipeline operator Transpetrol, the daily Pravda reports.  \par \par \uc2 Pravda, page 6  \par \par \uc2 PENSION SYSTEM CHANGES  \par \par \uc2 The new Social Affairs Minister Viera Tomanova is considering changing the pension system to make the private savings scheme a voluntary option, the daily Sme reports. Under the current rules, those who are entering the job market must sign up for private pension savings.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 1  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and for a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: reuters@editorial.sk  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b