\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown eases as mkt eyes PM talks with cbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2006\par 12:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, July 13 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown eased in nervous midday trade on Thursday as the market waited to see whether the government shows commitment to fiscal policies needed to meet the goal of adopting the euro in 2009.  Prime Minister Robert Fico and Finance Minister Jan Pociatek are scheduled to meet \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Ivan Sramko at 3 p.m. (1300 GMT) to debate Slovakia's euro adoption plans.  \par \par \uc2  The meeting comes after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the crown's decline on Wednesday as edgy mood on emerging markets and uncertainty over future economic policies pushed investors to dump \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets.  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had previously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the crown after Fico's leftist Smer party won a June 17 election, to beat a centre-right government praised by the markets for reforms, and created a coalition with two fringe factions.  \par \par \uc2 The cabinet has sent conflicting signals about its plans, increasing market nervousness that the euro adoption might be delayed.  \par \par \uc2  "A key issue is obviously whether the 2009 euro strategy will be kept," ING Bank said in a market note.  \par \par \uc2  The crown was at 38.640/660 to the euro as of 1030 GMT, after 38.600/605 at the open and compared with 38.700 where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected the NBS to keep guarding the crown as long as the euro target remains in place, keeping analysts guessing how long can the battle last if the weakening pressure persists.  \par \par \uc2  ING said the NBS had enough sources for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it estimated its reserves at a comfortable level covering 4.3 months of imports after Wednesday's action. But others disagreed.  \par \par \uc2  "Looking at rapidly declining amount of the reserves, questions are for how long the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , how much reserves usable left, and whether there are some institutional limits of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the crown is in ERM-2," said Miroslav Plojhar of Citibank Czech Republic. -----------------MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1030 GMT-------------------- Crown/euro <EURSKK=> 38.640/660 v. 38.450/500 on Wednesday Crown/dollar <SKK=>  30.400/450 v. 30.250/290 5-yr yield <SK5YT=RR> at 5.792/492 v. 5.675/373 9-yr yield <SK9YT=RR> at 5.715/514 v. 5.621/420 ----------------------------------------------------------------  ((Reporting by Martin Santa, writing by Peter Laca, Editing by Chris Pizzey; Reuters Messaging: martin.santa.reuters.com@reuters.net; Email: martin.santa@reuters.com; +421-2-5341-8402))  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CROWN-MIDDAY|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|CZS|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060713e27d001gj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
