\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Slovak cbank defends crown, market stays edgy  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Santa  \par \uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2006\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds announcement of PM meeting with c.bank, analysts quotes)  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Wednesday to defend the crown as an edgy mood on emerging markets and a shaky domestic political outlook pushed investors to dump more Slovak assets.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) bought crowns in several waves on the market after the unit fell by 0.6 percent to around 38.700 per euro, a far deeper drop than the neighbouring Polish zloty and the Hungarian forint, which were hit by weak regional sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been jumpy since a June 17 election in which the leftist Smer party beat the centre-right government, praised by the markets for economic reforms, and created a ruling coalition with two fringe factions.  \par \par \uc2 Apart from a bearish mood on emerging markets, which started in the spring with rising yields on major markets, investors also worry that the new Slovak government will loosen fiscal policy and miss the target of adopting the euro in 2009. "There is a lot of uncertainty on the political scene, and there are a lot of question marks about economic policies at this point," said CSOB Bank analyst Marek Gabris.  \par \par \uc2 "The market does not like uncertainty."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the unit to 38.400 at 1334 GMT, but market watchers said further weakness was possible. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came because of a too sharp weakening of the crown, the volatility of the crown was too sharp," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat said. He declined to elaborate.  \par \par \uc2 The NBS spent over a billion euros, according to dealer estimates, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the crown decline in June.  \par \par \uc2 CONFLICTING SIGNALS  \par \par \uc2 The government led by leftist Smer chief Robert Fico has sent conflicting signals about its plans, increasing market jitters over the feasibility of Slovakia's euro adoption plans.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Jan Pociatek said the goal of cutting the fiscal deficit and adopting the euro in 2009 will take priority over measures aimed at strengthening the welfare system.  \par \par \uc2 But Fico has already snubbed Pociatek's idea to scrap the plan of raising taxes for banks, which kept market watchers guessing whether the finance minister will be able to push through other fiscal ideas.  \par \par \uc2 The government office said Fico and Pociatek will meet with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Ivan Sramko on Thursday to debate entry to the euro zone.  \par \par \uc2 Apart from undesired crown volatility, which could affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability criterion for euro adoption assessment, the weak crown also conflicts with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plans to curb upward pressures on consumer prices.  \par \par \uc2 "It is obvious that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not agree with the current level of the crown, which also negatively influences inflation," said Lucia Steklacova, a senior analyst at ING Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue defending the crown as long as Slovakia does not alter the euro adoption schedule.  \par \par \uc2 "While the 2009 euro goal holds, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue to defend the crown in order to meet Maastricht criteria," Slovenska Sporitelna said in a market note.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CBANK (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|CZS|BNX|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060715e27c000ik\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
