\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to halt SKK weakening  \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2006\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quote, details)  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) said on Wednesday it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt a weakening of the crown <EURSKK=> amid an uncertain political outlook. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought crowns at around 38.710 per euro on the market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the unit to 38.600 at 1234 GMT. The crown traded at 38.480 late on Tuesday, and was at 38.510 per euro in early Wednesday trade.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came because of a too sharp weakening of the crown, the volatility of the crown was too sharp," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat said. He declined to give further details.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent more than a billion euros, according to dealers estimates, in two days of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of June.  \par \par \uc2 The crown has been under pressure since a June 17 election amid investor concerns a new leftist government will loosen fiscal discipline and endanger the goal of adopting the euro in 2009.  \par \par \uc2 Last week a coalition comprising the leftist Smer party, along with two fringe parties was appointed after Smer won the most votes, but not a majority, in a June 17 election.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Jan Pociatek told Reuters last week the goal of cutting the fiscal deficit and staying on track for adopting the euro in 2009 will take priority over measures aimed at strengthening the welfare system.  \par \par \uc2 But Smer leader Robert Fico immediately snubbed Pociatek's idea to scrap a plan of raising taxes for banks, which has raised fears in the market that the finance minister will not be able to push through other fiscal plans.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CBANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|CZS|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060715e27c000ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
