\par\par \b \uc2 Slovak crown seen under fire, mkt eyes govt steps  \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2006\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 3 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown was little changed to the euro on Monday but dealers expected it to weaken in the near term as the market awaited the first steps of an incoming leftist government.  \par \par \uc2 The crown traded at 38.420/450 to the euro as of 1030 GMT, after 38.440/460 late on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The crown has been volatile in the past few days after Smer said it would create a ruling coalition with two fringe parties. President Ivan Gasparovic is expected to name the new government on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the crown would stay under pressure due to uncertainty over Slovakia's target to adopt the euro in 2009.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect continued sell-off of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response," Slovenska Sporitelna said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market twice in the last two weeks of June to stop the crown fall.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Smer's intentions to lower value-added tax on some items and boost welfare spending could prevent a reduction of the fiscal deficit under 3 percent of GDP, which is required for adopting the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The crown showed no reaction to nomination of a businessman and a Smer deputy Jan Pociatek to the post of the finance minister as he is little known to financial markets.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said they needed to wait for his first comments to get some clues of the future fiscal policy. 