\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on June 30  \b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2006\par 09:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, June 30 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 ROBERT FICO TO MEET PRESIDENT GASPAROVIC  \par \par \uc2 Robert Fico, the leader of the leftist party Smer, will meet President Ivan Gasparovic to present him an outline of his new government (0745 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 DZURINDA TO HOLD NEWS CONFERENCE  \par \par \uc2 Outgoing Prime Minister Mikulas Dzurinda to hold a news conference (1100 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK TO RELEASE \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES DATA  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release its weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data (1200 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA UNDER FIRE FOR LEFTIST COALITION CHOICES  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia came under fire from investors and diplomats on Thursday after leftist party Smer chose two fringe parties for coalition talks, a move that could cool relations with its European Union partners. [ID:nL2935398]  \par \par \uc2 FINMIN UPS GDP, INFLATION FORECASTS  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak finance ministry raised its growth and inflation forecasts on Thursday but said the 2009 euro entry target was safe if a new government pursues correct fiscal policy. [ID:nL29488032]  \par \par \uc2 POLITICAL JITTERS HIT SKK, C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time in eight days on Thursday to halt a sliding crown amid fears the next government will rack up debt and defer plans to adopt the euro in 2009. [ID:nL29899242]  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SLOVAK\b0 \highlight\uc2  CROWN BOUNCES BACK ON C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown climbed back to firmer levels versus the euro on Thursday, after a 0.7 percent fall early in the session, benefiting from the second \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past seven days. [ID:nL29901254]  \par \par \uc2 COALITION DEAL SEEN ON SUNDAY  \par \par \uc2 Robert Fico expects Smer, the far-right Slovak National Party and the HZDS party of former authoritarian Prime Minister Vladimir Meciar to sign their coalition agreement on Sunday, the daily Sme reports.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 2  \par \par \uc2 SMER HAS 11 MINISTRIES  \par \par \uc2 The leftist party Smer will take eleven posts in the new government, the nationalists will take three ministries and HZDS will get two posts, daily Sme reports.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 1  \par \par \uc2 HZDS SAYS RESPECTS 2009 EURO ENTRY TARGET  \par \par \uc2 HZDS wants to enter the euro zone in 2009, in line with the current plan, Deputy Chairman Viliam Veteska told the daily Sme. HZDS Chairman Meciar has previously said euro adoption should be postponed until after 2010.  \par \par \uc2 Sme, page 5  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and for a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: reuters@editorial.sk  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\