\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Fed Stance Could Boost Markets  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2006\par 07:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT \par  \par 0900/0700 Hungary May Producer Price Index \par  \par 0900/0700 Hungary April Trade Deficit \par           Preliminary data: EUR187.6M vs EUR245M in Mar \par  \par 0830/0630 Hungary 1Q Current Account Deficit \par           Seen: EUR1.63B vs EUR1.49B in 4Q 2005 \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                   2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/PLN 4.0682-82  4.0761-21  -0.19  4.0877  4.0679   +5.85 \par EUR/HUF 282.61-91  282.75-00  -0.05  282.61  282.89  +12.00 \par EUR/CZK 28.465-95  28.455-85  +0.04  28.480  28.495   -2.08 \par EUR/SKK 38.330-80  38.370-10  -0.10  Untraded today   +1.32 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 THE POLISH ZLOTY:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Traders said the U.S. Federal Reserve Board's interest rate hike of 25bp as expected and its surprisingly dovish statement may relieve investors in emerging market assets, because the prospect of still more U.S. rates could have siphoned off funds from emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 The zloty weakened against the euro Thursday as the market awaited the U.S. rate decision, due after the close of trade in the Central and Eastern Europe region. Investors worried a rate hike would be accompanied by a hawkish statement. "We live in the world of rising rates, thus there's capital outflow from emerging markets," a trader said. The zloty clawed back some of its losses late Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the koruna. The National Bank of Slovakia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the koruna weakened amid political uncertainties. Late Thursday, the zloty traded at PLN4.0775 to the euro, from PLN4.0640 late Wednesday and PLN4.0955 earlier Thursday. Against the dollar, the zloty was at PLN3.2500, from PLN3.2392 late Wednesday and PLN3.2690 during trade Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 THE HUNGARIAN FORINT: CIB Bank analysts see little chance of a significant correction by the forint against the euro, given Hungary's "far from spotless" fiscal track record. "And the market still lacks confidence in the government's reform package," said. Traders said a Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate hike of between 50 and 75 basis points is needed to stem forint weakness and the inflationary pressure resulting from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide this week. "The longer the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waits, the higher it'll need to hike," a trader said, adding even this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only be a short-term panacea.  \par \par \uc2 The forint plunged against the euro Thursday in a move dealers said tested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's patience, leaving a rate hike looking inevitable. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at HUF182.10 early Thursday, sliding to HUF182.60 by midday and to HUF285.00 by late in the day. This compared with HUF280.30 late Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to weaken despite the boost to other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Zoltan J. Gal, state secretary at the prime minister's office, attributed the sharp weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to regional factors. He refused to comment on whether the government had been in consultation with the National Bank of Hungary in the wake of Thursday's drastic weakening. Traders said the forint's weakness was also likely due to investor repositioning before the U.S. rate decision late Thursday, since comments pointing to further U.S. rate hikes from the Fed after its rate decision would be severely negative for Hungary. Hungary, which is struggling with the widest budget deficit in the European Union, could see a further deterioration in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds if portfolio investors decide to withdraw from forint assets, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 THE CZECH KORUNA: Short term, the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to leave interest rates on hold, as it did Thursday. CIB Bank analysts predict the bank will next hike rates in the third quarter.  \par \par \uc2 The koruna weakened against the euro Thursday in the wake of the bank's decision to keep its key two-week repo rate unchanged at 2%, or 75 basis points below the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's corresponding rate. The weakness was also driven by the weakness of the Hungarian forint and Slovak koruna against the euro. The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  clawed back some losses late in the day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  koruna. Late Thursday, the koruna traded at CZK28.520 to the euro, from CZK28.390 late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLISH BONDS are likely to react to the U.S. interest rate decision and accompanying statement in line with an expected rise in German bunds early Friday, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Polish government bonds were little changed Thursday, weakening early in the session, before clawing back losses after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  koruna. Late Thursday, the yield on the two-year bond was at 5.07%, unchanged from late Wednesday. The five-year bond yield was also unchanged at 5.60%, while the 10-year bond yield was at 5.68%, from 5.73%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARIAN BONDS: U.S. Federal Reserve comments late Thursday are interpreted as favorable for emerging markets, and Hungarian bonds could recover Friday, a trader said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungarian government bonds weakened Thursday as the forint fell against the euro, making a Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate hike look inevitable, the trader said. Yields on the short end of the curve rose between 20 and 25 basis points compared with late Wednesday, while yields on the long end rose between 15 and 20 basis points.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH BONDS: The 25 basis point U.S. interest rate hike Thursday should strengthen core bond markets including German bunds Friday, with the positive influence spilling over into trade of Czech paper, CSOB analyst Jan Cermak said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Czech government bonds were little changed Thursday. Trade was light until the Czech National Bank announced it was keeping its key interest rate on hold. Yields on the short end of the curve fell by between three and four basis points immediately after the bank's announcement, although they later crept back up. The Czech rate decision had little effect on the long end of the curve. Long-dated bonds tend not to move in tandem with those in core markets such as German bunds. "There seemed to be some bullishness on the steep end of the curve," Cermak said. Late Thursday, the average yield on the benchmark 10-year bond was at 4.11%, from 4.10% late Wednesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG20                   2842.29    loss   8.19  dn  0.3% \par BUX                    20390.31    gain 215.14  up  1.1% \par PX                      1346.30    gain  25.30  up  1.9% \par  \par DJ STOXX EU Enlarged 15   2498.97  loss  13.05   dn 0.5% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: The market may bounce back Friday, with local funds likely to push the WIG20 index up to achieve a successful close to the end of the month, the quarter and the half-year period, a trader said. That is, "Unless we see some huge supply by foreign players after the Fed's (interest rate) decision," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The WIG20 ended down 0.3% at 2842.29 Thursday as some foreign investors took profits after the index's two-day rally. "Foreign sellers are the major culprits," the broker said. Among losers, TPSA ended down 2.7%, PKN down 2.7% and Prokom down 1.2%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Upward momentum is expected to last, even if the Fed decides to hike interest rates. "The sellers are still here, but they are not as strong as in the past weeks," an EIB trader said. Even if the market opens lower Friday - since Federal Reserve comments might be negative for emerging markets - Budapest stocks are set to rise further later in the day, he said..  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BUX index ended up 1.1% at 20390.31 Thursday as buying interest returned after several weeks of heavy selling, mirroring a recovery by U.S. stocks, the trader said. Among gainers, OTP Bank ended up 2.6%, Magyar Telekom up 2.5% and Egis up 4.4%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Further gains by CEZ shares is possible Friday, given the shares are proving attractive to foreign buyers this week, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The PX index ended up 1.9% at 1346.3 Thursday, driven mainly by a rally by CEZ shares, which ended up 4.1% with a volume of almost CZK3 billion. "The only reason for the rise on the index was foreign buyers on CEZ," an Atlantik Financial Markets trader said. With the exception of Zentiva, which ended up 3.5%, most stocks were little changed. "Zentiva is the same story as CEZ - foreign buyers see opportunity," he said. Among stocks moving sideways in thin trade were Philip Morris, which ended up 0.6%, Komercni Banka, up 0.1%, and Cesky Telecom, up 0.7%. [ 06-30-06 0101ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OVERNIGHT NEWS \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The lower chamber of Czech parliament failed to elect a speaker Thursday, prolonging the political deadlock created by this month's general elections.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Poland's premier asked former Finance Minister Zyta Gilowska to become his deputy Thursday, inviting her to rejoin the government after she resigned last week over allegations she collaborated with the country's communist-era secret police. Gilowska was seen as a leading advocate for fiscal responsibility in Prime Minister Kazimierz Marcinkiewicz's government and news of her departure triggered a sell-off of Polish zlotys and Treasury bonds. Markets quickly recovered, however, after Pawel Wojciechowski, a pro-market, U.S.-trained economist, was named as her replacement.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Slovakia's Smer-Social Democracy Party and its two right-wing coalition partners have agreed on the distribution of ministerial seats in the country's new government, party leader Robert Fico said on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Romania's prime minister on Thursday proposed withdrawing his country's 890 troops from Iraq, citing security concerns and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's cost, but the president called the idea "unacceptable."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Serbia's government is drafting an "action plan" to locate and capture top war crimes suspect Gen. Ratko Mladic, a senior government official said Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -The sharp weakening of the Hungarian forint is due to regional factors, Zoltan J. Gal, state secretary at the prime minister's office, said Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Susannah Rodgers, Dow Jones Newswires; 44-208-789-8467; susannah.rodgers@dowjones.com [ 06-30-06 0102ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020060630e26u00005\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
