\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown bounces back on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2006\par 16:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, June 29 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown climbed back to firmer levels versus the euro on Thursday, after a 0.7 percent fall early in the session, benefiting from the second \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past seven days.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 38.300/320 to the euro as 1400 GMT, slightly firmer from 38.380/400 at the open but weaker from 38.155/185 late on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market when the crown fell to 38.475 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 Its fall was driven by investors' worries about an announcement that the leftist Smer party will invite the party of former authoritarian Prime Minister Vladimir Meciar and far-right nationalists to form a government after election earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 "This means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably defend the 38.50-38.55 per euro range in the near term and protect the crown from more losses," Slovenska Sporitelna wrote in a market note.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which were accumulated during massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a strong crown in 2004 and 2005," it added.  \par \par \uc2 Investors fear a Smer government with the fringe parties, lukewarm to the 2009 euro entry plan, could loosen fiscal discipline and expand public deficits.  \par \par \uc2 Smer chief Robert Fico is due to meet President Ivan Gasparovic at 0745 GMT on Friday to present the set-up of the incoming government.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expected the crown to move between 38.200-38.500 per euro in the short term. ----------------MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1420 GMT-------------------- Crown/euro <EURSKK=> at 38.395/410 vs. 38.155/185 (-0.53 pct) Crown/dollar <SKK=> at 30.552/600 vs. 38.465/510 (-0.22 pct) 3-yr yield <SK5YT=RR> at 5.514/215 vs 4.914/614 9-yr yield <SK9YT=RR> at 5.550/390 vs 4.960/760 --------------------------------------------------------------  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CROWN-CLOSE|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|CZS|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060702e26t000bw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
