\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown stabilises after c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2006\par 17:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, June 22 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown weathered a bearish regional mood on Thursday better than its neighbours following supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, dealers said. The crown ended at 38.230/250 to the euro, down from 38.190/220 late on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Other central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell by more, with the Polish zloty losing 0.4 percent and the forint weakening by half a percent.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said investors in the Slovak market were wary of approaching 38.550 per euro, the point where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought crowns directly on the market on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Emerging markets are suffering because rising yields in major markets are drawing investors away.  \par \par \uc2 But even if the emerging markets stabilise, the Slovak crown will have little room to strengthen until the the next government is formed, traders say.  \par \par \uc2 "There wasn't much interest in the market today and that could last for weeks," said Boris Somorovsky, a trader at Tatra Banka. "In the meantime we'll probably follow regional swings, but within a narrow range."  \par \par \uc2 The leftist Smer party won a weekend election and it now leads negotiations to form a government. The market will be edgy as long as participation of two fringe parties in the ruling coalition remains a possible option.  \par \par \uc2 The crown fell to seven-month lows on Wednesday after Smer signalled it might rule with far-right nationalists and a party of former autocratic Prime Minister Vladimir Meciar.  \par \par \uc2 Smer has also held talks with two centre-right parties, the Christian Democrats and the ethnic Hungarians.  \par \par \uc2 Investors fear a Smer-led government with Meciar and the nationalists, will push up the fiscal deficit, scare off investors and postpone plans to adopt the euro in 2009.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1425 GMT--------------------\par Crown/euro <EURSKK=>  at 38.230/250 vs 38.190/220 on Wednesday\par Crown/dollar <SKK=>   at 30.428/488 vs 30.200/250\par 5-yr yield <SK5YT=RR> at 4.706/405 vs 4.715/415\par 9-yr yield <SK9YT=RR> at 4.809/610 vs 4.800/600\par --------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CROWN-CLOSE|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|CZS|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060625e26m000c4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
