\par\par \b \uc2 Czech crown holds firm, bonds rebound from selloff  \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2006\par 10:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, June 22 (Reuters) - The Czech crown held ground versus the euro on Thursday after recovering from a two-month low in the previous session, as sentiment in central European markets brightened after a \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The crown traded barely changed on the day at 28.380 per euro <0#EURCZK=> by 0835 GMT. It had hit a low of 28.585 on Thursday before the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to prop up its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  [ID:nL2119218].  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak move, responding to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide through its central rate in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism, helped boost other regional units after a month-long selling on concern global credit tightening would slash their allure to investors.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the robust, more than 7 percent growth in the Czech economy, a low inflation outlook and credible monetary policy should allow the crown to continue outperforming central European peers. It is 2.5 percent firmer in the year-to-date.  \par \par \uc2 "In our view... the crown should remain a relative safe haven likely to outperform other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jon Harrison, market strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \par \par \uc2 Local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds <0#CZBMK=> rebounded after Wednesday's heavy sell-off triggered by the news of poor investor interest in the sale of a 9-year government debt tranche <CZ9YT=RR>.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year benchmark debt yield <CZ10YT=RR> fell from a 1-1/2-year high, shedding 7 basis points to 4.13/4.10 percent, with its spread over the euro zone equivalent narrowing from a 6-month high.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Wednesday's auction failed to draw enough buyers for the offer due to this month's crown drop and rising global interest rates [ID:nL2141861].   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0835 GMT -----------------\par  Crown/euro <EURCZK=>       last deals at 28.380     (-0.05 pct)\par  Crown/dollar <CZK=>                   at 22.395 bid (-0.11 pct)\par   5-year yield due Oct 2010 <CZ5YT=RR>     3.72 pct bid (-4 bps)\par  10-year yield due Jan 2016 <CZ10YT=RR>    4.13 pct bid (-7 bps)\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5-yr CZK/EUR mid yield spread <DE114147=> -6 bps (vs -1) 10-yr CZK/EUR mid yield spread <DE113529=> 11 bps (vs 20)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Current levels versus prior domestic close at 1500 GMT ---------------------------------------------------------------  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CZECH-CROWN-MORNING|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|CZS|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060625e26m00050\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
