\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown flat after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , politics key  \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2006\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, June 22 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown held stable on Thursday morning after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped its fall in the previous session, and dealers said the market was awaiting a fresh impetus from government talks.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday after post-election uncertainty and a bearish mood on emerging markets pushed the crown through its central rate in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism.  \par \par \uc2 The crown traded at 38.180/190 to the euro at 0800 GMT, little changed from 38.190/220 late on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The crown has been falling since the leftist Smer party won an election on Saturday and started government talks with two fringe parties. Investors feared such a government would loosen fiscal policy and delay euro adoption beyond 2009.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought crowns at around 38.550 to the euro on Wednesday, and local banks estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume was up to 300 million euros.  \par \par \uc2 "Unless the future government announces a euro (adoption) delay, which we see as unlikely at this stage, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably defend the territory around 38.55 per euro as the 2009 euro goal would be still valid," Slovenska Sporitelna said in market note.  \par \par \uc2 Smer leader Robert Fico said on Wednesday he might continue in coalition talks with two centre-right members of the previous government, and their cabinet participation would be positive for the crown as they could prevent radical changes to reforms, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stay nervous until the future government is formed and presents its programme, which could take several weeks.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------------MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0800 GMT--------------------\par Crown/euro <EURSKK=>  at 38.180/190 vs 38.190/220 on Wednesday\par Crown/dollar <SKK=>   at 30.170/215 vs 30.200/250\par 5-yr yield <SK5YT=RR> at 4.716/415 vs 4.715/415\par 9-yr yield <SK9YT=RR> at 4.798/600 vs 4.800/600\par --------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CROWN-OPEN|LANGEN|Table|CZS|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060625e26m0004n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
