\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown below ERM-2 parity, c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Laca  \par \uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2006\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2   (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, June 21 (Reuters) - Post-election jitters and a sour mood on emerging markets pushed the Slovak crown below its central rate in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism on Wednesday, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  The crown <EURSKK=> <SKK=> has weakened sharply since the leftist Smer party won a general election on Saturday and started talks on forming a government with two fringe parties, an option analysts have called the worst case scenario to emerge from the election.  \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the crown fell below its central rate of 38.455 to the euro in midday trading for the first time since the central European country entered the waiting room for the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November 2005.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) stepped in and bought crowns at around 38.550 to the euro, dealers said. The NBS confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but declined to give any levels for its deals.  \par \par \uc2  "The reason was a significant weakening of the crown in recent days, which we considered unjustified by economic fundamentals," NBS spokesman Igor Barat said. "We will remain ready to react if needed in the future."  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the crown to 38.300 per euro. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to buy the crown on the market in several waves. The crown is now trading some 4.2 percent below its all-time highs of 36.925 it hit on March 1.  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall comes after Smer leader Robert Fico said he did not see any major obstacles to forming a government with the centre-left HZDS party of former authoritarian Prime Minister Vladimir Meciar and the far-right nationalists.  \par \par \uc2  EURO WORRIES  \par \par \uc2  Investors worry a Smer-led government, especially if joined by the nationalists and Meciar, would raise spending, spook foreign companies and delay euro zone entry from 2009 as intended.  \par \par \uc2  "The market got scared of the possibility of a Smer coalition with HZDS and the nationalists," said Lucia Steklacova, a senior analyst at ING Bank. "Such an alternative would probably mean looser fiscal policy, higher inflation and subsequently higher interest rates."  \par \par \uc2  Smer will hold talks later on Wednesday with three centre-right parties that formed the previous government of Prime Minister Mikulas Dzurinda.  \par \par \uc2  But the market reacted negatively to Fico's statements that ruling with Dzurinda's junior partners, the ethnic Hungarians and Christian Democrats, was not his most attractive option.  \par \par \uc2  Such a government would be welcomed by the market as it was expected to have a more moderate economic agenda, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2  Fico, whose party won a third of parliament's 150 seats, has pledged to cancel a business-friendly flat 19 percent tax rate and undo other reforms introduced by Dzurinda's cabinet to ease the pain of economic transformation from the past four years.  \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the turmoil could last weeks as Fico faces tough talks to forge a viable coalition. Dzurinda could still stay in power if Smer fails to find enough allies among the six parties that have entered parliament.  \par \par \uc2  "A combination of Smer, HZDS and the nationalists would quite possibly lead to a delay of euro adoption from the targeted year 2009, which would be negative for the market," said Slovenska Sporitelna analyst Michal Musak.     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CROWN (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|CZS|RBN|BNX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060621e26l000n2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
