\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Oct 14  \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2005\par 08:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Oct 14 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK TO PUBLISH RESERVES DATA  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to release its weekly foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data (1200 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO SUPPORT CROWN  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to support the ailing crown, with analysts saying the move was aimed at safeguarding inflation goals set for euro adoption.  \par \par \uc2 HIGHWAY TOLL SYSTEM TENDER  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia plans a tender for the supplier of a highway toll collection system worth up to 13 billion crowns ($400 million) in the next few months, the National Highway Company said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 CROWN UP AFTER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown <EURSKK=> rebounded from five-month lows versus the euro on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the market to support the falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market when the crown fell to 39.200 per euro, its weakest level since May. The action pulled the crown back through the psychological level of 39.000 per euro, and the unit closed at 38.940/960.  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators,  \par \par \uc2 see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets                         [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch                        [TOP/EAST]\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on Oct 14|LANGEN|Table|CZS|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|REVU|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051014e1ae000gd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
