\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown off 5-month lows after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2005\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Oct 13 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown <EURSKK=> rebounded from five-month lows versus the euro on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the market to support its falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market when the crown fell to 39.200 per euro, its weakest level since May. The action pulled the crown back through the psychological level of 39.000 per euro, and the unit closed at 38.940/960. "The NBS (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) clearly showed its determination to prevent further crown depreciation that does not correspond with Slovakia's good macroeconomic indicators," VUB Bank said in a market note.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown has been under pressure in the past few weeks, hit by a domestic government crisis followed by economic and political turmoil in neighbouring central European states.  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia has shown fast economic growth and rising inflows of foreign direct investment in the past few years, but the crown is frequently influenced by capital flows on bigger markets in central Europe.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the crown could move near the 39.0-per-euro mark again if the mood in the region further worsened, but they added the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a good support level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We expect gradual crown appreciation in the coming months due to the favourable macroeconomic trends, though investors' sentiment towards central European markets remained a risk factor," VUB said. -------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1500 GMT------------------ Crown/euro <EURSKK=> at 38.940/960 vs 38.860/960 on Wednesday Crown/dollar <SKK=> at 32.605/655 vs. 32.300/350 5-yr yield <SK5YT=RR> at 3.285/2.986 pct vs 3.212/2.912 pct 9-yr yield <SK9YT=RR> at 3.378/177 pct vs 3.214/3.085 pct ---------------------------------------------------------------  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-CROWN-CLOSE|LANGEN|Table|CZS|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051013e1ad001hw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
