\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support falling crown  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Laca  \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2005\par 14:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Writes through with analyst comments)  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, Oct 13 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to support the ailing crown, with analysts saying the move was aimed at safeguarding inflation goals set for euro adoption.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown has been under pressure in the past few weeks, hit by a domestic government crisis followed by economic and political turmoil in neighbouring central European states.  \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) stepped into the market on Thursday when its unit fell to 39.200 per euro, the weakest level since May. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action designed to support the crown in more than five months.  \par \par \uc2 "The reason for the action was that the development of the exchange rate did not correspond with economic fundamentals," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat said.  \par \par \uc2 "We have stated in the past that we will be ready to correct excessive movements which are not in line with developments of the economy, and this is still valid."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action brought the crown through the psychological level of 39.000 per euro, and the unit traded at 38.910/930 to the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in afternoon activity.  \par \par \uc2 The NBS last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown at the end of April when capital flight from emerging markets pushed central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply down.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the opposite direction in the first three months of the year when it fought hard to slow down the crown's rapid appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 INFLATION IN MIND  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not elaborate on the reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but analysts said the monetary body wanted to prevent risks to its inflation goals that could arise if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too weak for too long.  \par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate channel has the fastest impact on inflation," said Maria Feherova, senior analyst at Slovakia's largest bank, Slovenska Sporitelna.  \par \par \uc2 The NBS has a target to keep inflation under 2.5 percent at the end of next year, which would be slowing price growth from the annual 4.3 percent expected in December in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 The end-2007 inflation limit is 2.0 percent, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects will be enough to meet the euro adoption condition.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts have long expected the Slovak crown to firm as the new European Union member has shown fast economic growth and rising inflows of foreign direct investment in the past few years.  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia has also become the frontrunner for euro adoption among the four largest new EU members from central Europe as its neighbours struggle with ballooning fiscal deficits.  \par \par \uc2 But the crown is frequently influenced by capital flows on bigger markets in the region and it often follows movements of the Polish zloty or Hungarian forint.  \par \par \uc2 "The crown weakening did not come because of a worsening of Slovakia's economic picture," Feherova said. "The recent moves were caused solely by external factors."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SLOVAKIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|CZS|ABN|M|D|BNX|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051013e1ad0013l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
