\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on June 9  \b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2005\par 08:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, June 9 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 STATS OFFICE TO RELEASE Q1 GDP DATA  \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will release the first quarter GDP data.  \par \par \uc2 STATS OFFICE TO RELEASE H1 GDP FORECAST  \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will release its GDP forecast for the first half of 2005.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK WAGE GROWTH RISKS EASE IN APRIL - CBANKER  \par \par \uc2 Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice-Governor Martin Barto said on Wednesday that risks for inflation associated with fast wage growth eased in April, but remain a concern over the longer-term.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK RETAIL SALES GROWTH SLOWS IN APRIL  \par \par \uc2 Slovak retail sales rose by a real 6.8 percent year-on-year in April, down from 8.1 percent annual growth in March, the Slovak Statistics Office said.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK APRIL INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT REBOUNDS  \par \par \uc2 Slovak industrial output rose real 5.1 percent year-on-year in April, after a revised 2.0 percent annual decline in the previous month, the Slovak Statistics Office said.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK APRIL CONSTRUCTION OUTPUT +17.9 PCT Y/Y  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's construction output rose by 17.9 percent on the year in April, up from 8.1 percent growth registered in March, the Slovak Statistics Office said.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA PLANS TO SELL 66 PCT IN TWO MAJOR AIRPORTS  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak government plans to sell 66 percent in the country's two international airports by the end of this year, the transportation minister said.  \par \par \uc2 MAN AG CUTS LIST OF SITES FOR TRUCK PLANT - REPORT  \par \par \uc2 German industrial group MAN AG has narrowed the list of potential sites for its planned manufacturing plant to Krakow in Poland and Kosice in Slovakia, German business magazine Capital reported.  \par \par \uc2 EU INCREASES AUSTRIAN, SLOVAK WHEAT EXPORT TENDERS  \par \par \uc2 The European Union has increased the amount of the wheat available for export via tenders from Austrian and \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stores, the Official Journal said in its latest edition.  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50> Other related news:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Slovak equities      [SK-E]  E.Europe equities           [.CEE]\par  Slovak money         [SK-M]  Czech debt                  [CZ-D]\par  Slovak Indicators  [SK-ECI]  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [EMRG/FRX]\par  Eastern European     [EEU]   All emerging markets        [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks           [HOT]   Stock markets                [STX]\par  Market debt news     [DBT]   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news                   [FRX]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets                         [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch                        [TOP/EAST]\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on June 9|LANGEN|Table|CZS|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|REVU|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050609e169000fy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppi