\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on May 26  \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2005\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, May 26 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 FOREIGN MINISTRY NEWS CONFERENCE  \par \par \uc2 The foreign ministry will hold a news conference on a meeting of foreign ministers of the Central European Initiative scheduled for May 28-29.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAK C.BANK REJECTS FEARS EURO WILL HURT GROWTH  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is convinced euro adoption will help accelerate economic growth, Governor Jan Sramko said on Wednesday, rejecting the cautious approach of some central bankers in the neighbouring Czech Republic.  \par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA SAYS KIA EYEING BIGGER OUTPUT IN NEW PLANT  \par \par \uc2 South Korean car maker Kia Motors could raise the output target at its new Slovak plant to 300,000 units a year as it expects improved European market conditions, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  ministry spokesman said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SLOVAK\b0 \highlight\uc2  WHEAT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  OFFERS RISE TO 239,000 T  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's wheat \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  offers currently stand at 239,000 tonnes, up from 201,000 at the end of April, rising near the maximum expected amount for this year, said the state purchasing agency.  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see <G7TODAY>. For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click [SK/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 534